# 10-partitioning run 2026-09-27T13:15:36Z
== fresh Postgres (docker compose down -v && up) ==
 Container 10-partitioning-postgres-1 Healthy 
setup: orders PARTITION BY HASH (customer_id) into 4 partitions (orders_p0..orders_p3)

## 1. Postgres routes each row
   concept: the app inserts into the parent table; Postgres hashes customer_id and stores the row in one partition
   alice keyboard -> orders_p1 (id 1)
   alice mouse    -> orders_p1 (id 2)
   bob   screen   -> orders_p2 (id 3)
   carol desk     -> orders_p1 (id 4)
   dave  chair    -> orders_p0 (id 5)
   erin  lamp     -> orders_p0 (id 6)

## 2. Partition pruning
   concept: a query that filters on the partition key only touches the matching partition
     Bitmap Heap Scan on orders_p1 orders
       Recheck Cond: (customer_id = 'alice'::text)
       ->  Bitmap Index Scan on orders_p1_pkey
             Index Cond: (customer_id = 'alice'::text)

## 3. No key, no pruning
   concept: without the partition key every partition is scanned (in sharding: every shard is queried)
     Append
       ->  Seq Scan on orders_p0 orders_1
             Filter: (item = 'lamp'::text)
       ->  Seq Scan on orders_p1 orders_2
             Filter: (item = 'lamp'::text)
       ->  Seq Scan on orders_p2 orders_3
             Filter: (item = 'lamp'::text)
       ->  Seq Scan on orders_p3 orders_4
             Filter: (item = 'lamp'::text)

## 4. Uniqueness must include the key
   concept: each partition has its own index, so Postgres cannot enforce uniqueness on id alone
   rejected: unique constraint on partitioned table must include all partitioning columns

## 5. Still one server
   concept: one transaction can span partitions and rolls back atomically; after sharding (11) this is no longer true
   rejected: null value in column "item" of relation "orders_p2" violates not-null constraint
   alice's cable rows after rollback: 0

## 6. Changing the key moves the row
   concept: UPDATE of customer_id deletes from one partition and inserts into another, in the same transaction
   erin's lamp now belongs to frank -> orders_p2

